# Cursor Rules for MultiGender Hebrew Text Designer

## Version Management
- **CRITICAL**: Every time you commit changes, automatically increment the version number in `src/index.html`
- Version format: `v{major}.{minor}.{patch}` (e.g., v1.3.0)
- Version increment rules:
  - **Patch** (+0.0.1): Bug fixes, small improvements, CSS tweaks, minor text changes
  - **Minor** (+0.1.0): New features, UI improvements, significant functionality additions
  - **Major** (+1.0.0): Breaking changes, complete rewrites, major architecture changes

## Version Location
- Version is displayed in `<span class="version-small">` inside `<div class="footer-version">` at the bottom of `src/index.html`
- Always update the version before committing
- Include version change in commit message

## Commit Message Format
```
[Type]: Brief description

- Change 1
- Change 2
- Version: v{old} → v{new}
```

## Code Style
- Use modular JavaScript (CONFIG, Utils, FontManager, etc.)
- Maintain mobile-first responsive design
- Always test font loading and canvas rendering
- Keep consistent naming conventions
- Use CSS variables for theming

## MultiGender Hebrew Specifics
- Always use `AlefMultiGenderHebrew` font
- Support special characters: ׭׬׌׎׫׊׏׋׉׮׍׈
- Ensure proper RTL/LTR text handling
- Test on both desktop and mobile
- Maintain canvas text centering

## File Structure
- `src/index.html` - Main page with version display
- `src/script.js` - Modular JavaScript
- `src/styles.css` - Responsive CSS with themes
- `src/fonts/` - Font files

## Testing Requirements
- Test text alignment on mobile and desktop
- Verify font loading works
- Check theme switching
- Ensure responsive layout
- Test special character rendering

## Never Do
- Skip version increment on commits
- Break mobile responsiveness
- Remove MultiGender Hebrew font support
- Create new files without explicit need
- Ignore linter warnings
